Use case: stylized-concept. ONE new production-ready isolated RGBA in-game sprite for Passagem das Amarras, industrial logistics passage east/southeast of Forjas toward Engrenopolis, never a new forge or residential/dock district. Reference original_visual_benchmark.png controls exact hand-painted weathered rendering, camera and light. Elevated orthographic 3/4 TOP-DOWN from SOUTH looking NORTH, no diagonal isometric yaw, roofs/top surfaces dominate, short south faces. Diffuse upper-left daytime light; tight local contact shadow only at real feet. No surrounding ground/floor replacement tile, water scenery, people/text/night aesthetics. Preserve alpha0 outside physical object and through openings. Target10% clear extraction margin, all chains/flanges/footings complete, no clipped edges. Doors24-28px gameplay; furnace canvas340x293px, tall exhaust add-on184x321px; open smithy189x133; service vessel189x126; cargo capstan120-160px wide; supported connector100x36, short service catwalk220x56px. Numeric dimensions below refer to visible object excluding transparent margins. Visible repairs, friction wear, active maintained use; no random disconnected chain or abandoned ornamental wreck.

PRODUCTION CONSTRAINTS:
- exact elevated 3/4 top-down perspective matching the current Ferrugem Baixa sprites;
- same lighting direction as the current map assets;
- readable at gameplay zoom, not concept-art-only;
- same rendering language as current hand-painted sprites;
- transparent background for extraction;
- clean silhouette;
- clear ground contact;
- visible foundation, feet, supports or anchoring where appropriate;
- no floating elements;
- no cinematic perspective;
- no text;
- no characters.
MATERIALS:
- dark stone, rusted iron, copper, patched timber, worn steel plates, soot, oil, grime.
AREA IDENTITY:
- Passagem das Amarras is not a forge district;
- it is an industrial passage / transfer / anchoring / structural support area;
- less furnace heat, more transport, restraint, tension, maintenance and edge infrastructure.
QA REQUIREMENTS:
- every asset must show how it touches or anchors to the ground;
- every suspended or structural element needs visible support;
- if chains/cables exist, they must have believable origin points;
- if the asset interfaces with terrain edge or canal, show retaining or anchoring logic.

MODULAR CONNECTION RULES:
- explicit complete connection lugs, bolts, shackle/chain endpoints;
- align ports to screen axes where specified;
- no decorative floating chains, no long chains leaving frame;
- contact shadows contained beneath real footings, no broad brown haze;
- new variants differ in structural function, not just color;
- no duplicated generic pipe, bridge, crane, capstan or electrical pole.
ASSET: ONE FLAT LOGISTICS WEAR DECAL, only sparse dark chain-drag arcs, two parallel cargo wheel abrasion traces, a few tiny rusty metallic dust specks and scratched anchor-ring contact circles. Target footprint210x90px, wheel separation36px, chain gouges2-4px thick at gameplay size beside24px door. No painted stones, dirt backdrop, floor tiles or replacement ground texture, no actual chains or cargo objects, no raised geometry. Stains/deposits on existing receiving stone, mostly translucent with alpha0 gaps and soft edges. Underlying game stone texture must show through. Ground contact means scratches flat on receiving surface, no fake floating shadow. More restraint/traction wear than soot or forge heat. Reusable route overlay, one contiguous modular decal not atlas.

